{"step":"proof.cleanup","gatewayStopped":true,"disposableStateRemoved":true}
```

</details>

Closes #203956

## What Problem This Solves

Session progress updates can stop after a model copies internal bookkeeping from the previous assessment. The observer rejects the response and can stop asking for updates for that run.

## User Impact

The session observer can continue reporting progress when a model echoes the prior assessment fields.

## Why This Change Was Made

Give the model a previous assessment containing only the fields accepted in a new assessment. Keep Gateway revisions, run and session identity, and timestamps out of the prompt. The response validator stays strict.

## Evidence

- On upstream `b62eec8f6`, the regression kept revision 1 instead of publishing a second live digest. This change passes that regression and all 39 tests across the observer, model, and completion suites. Core typecheck, formatting, lint, and the runtime build passed. The built revision was `db947a22b`.
- An isolated, built Gateway reproduced the failure using a model fixture that returns the previous assessment. The base retried the echoed metadata and disabled the observer. The fixed Gateway published two live digests and a terminal digest. The repeated observer request contained only `headline`, `assessment`, `health`, and `planProgress` in `previousDigest`.
- The same isolated Gateway also accepted a subsequent assessment from a live Qwen3.8 Flash utility inference. The loopback fixture drove the agent's synthetic file reads. The relay forwarded the Gateway's observer prompt to the real utility model and returned its text to the Gateway's unchanged validator. The reporter's Claude Haiku CLI route was not exercised.
- An independent local review compared `b62eec8f6..db947a22b` and found no behavioral blocker. It confirmed that the committed prompt and response schema reject the baseline echo and accept the projected one.

### Live Gateway proof

The test driver started each built `openclaw.mjs gateway run` on loopback in a fresh state directory, subscribed to WebSocket `session.observer` events, and sent a chat turn that read six synthetic files. The fixture repeated the Gateway's actual prior assessment. In the live check, the relay used the actual provider response text for the next assessment. Values below are extracted from the captured trace; filesystem paths, request IDs, and addresses are omitted.

```text
BASE b62eec8f65876f8566e0ab192c58b12db650cc69 — echo fixture
  second request.previousDigest keys: agentId, assessment, headline, health, planProgress, revision, runId, sessionKey, updatedAt
  [session-observer] session observer disabled after consecutive failures
    consecutiveFailures=2: session observer returned invalid JSON twice
  session.observer {"headline":"Checking fixtures","health":"on-track","revision":1}
  session.observer {"headline":"Fixture checks finished.","health":"done","revision":2}

FIXED db947a22b2743e7b5d807d9bc91e8dfd66c8a248 — same echo fixture
  second request.previousDigest keys: assessment, headline, health, planProgress
  session.observer {"headline":"Checking fixtures","health":"on-track","revision":1}
  session.observer {"headline":"Checking fixtures","health":"on-track","revision":2}
  session.observer {"headline":"Checking fixtures","health":"done","revision":3}

FIXED db947a22b2743e7b5d807d9bc91e8dfd66c8a248 — live utility replay
  repeated request.previousDigest keys: assessment, headline, health, planProgress
  utility response: {"utilityRoute":"qwen3.8-flash","http":200}
  observed request/response: {"keys":["assessment","headline","health","planProgress"],"noteCount":9,"confirmedRealReply":true}
  session.observer {"headline":"Checking fixtures","health":"on-track","revision":1}
  session.observer {"headline":"Reading fixture files","health":"on-track","revision":2}
  session.observer {"headline":"Reading fixture files","health":"done","revision":3}
  chat terminal state: final
```

