## What Problem This Solves

A scheduled job can receive delivery instructions after OpenClaw has admitted its task. Appending those instructions to the task can change its admission generation before the first tool call.

## User Impact

Scheduled jobs keep their original task and transcript prompt while the runner supplies delivery instructions appropriate to the tools available for that turn.

## Why This Change Was Made

Cron now passes delivery guidance as per-turn runtime context. CLI and embedded execution resolve it once the available tools are known. For plugin-owned transport, the host resolves the guidance conservatively before dispatch. Heartbeat and session-event producers remain open under #172031.

